  "body": "Part of #3663 (the tool library dialog). A follow-up of the component track (#3644, #3645, #4271, #4280).\n\n## What happens\n\nA project or a `.camtools` library from before the component track opens as before: each tool keeps its record, its holder and its body. But each tool is standalone: it has no component stack. To link a tool to components (holder, collet, insert), the user builds the stack by hand in the tool tab (\"Add component\", then \"Apply stack\"). For a library with many tools, this is too much work.\n\n## Expected\n\nA command **Convert to components** for the selected tools, or for all tools in the document or in My library:\n\n- For each tool, find a stack that gives the same tool: the holder from the tool's library holder (built-in, or a user holder), a collet that fits the shank where the holder is a collet chuck, and the tool itself as the cutting item. Indexable tools use the insert and the body when the tool record names them.\n- Show a preview before anything changes: one row for each tool with the proposed stack, and the result:\n  - \"same\": the stack derives the same tool record and gauge length;\n  - \"different\": the stack derives other values (list the differences);\n  - \"no match\": the reason by name (no holder, no collet for this shank, no insert).\n- Apply only the rows that the user selects, default the \"same\" rows. All selected rows land in **one** undo step.\n- A tool whose stack would change its record is never converted without the user's selection. The tool record and the posted G-code of a converted tool stay the same.\n- An MCP tool for the same command, with a dry-run that returns the preview.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests: a library of standalone tools converts; the \"same\" rows land in one undo step and undo restores every tool exactly; a \"different\" row shows its differences and is not applied by default; a \"no match\" row names its reason; the posted program of a converted tool does not change.\n- Before and after screenshots of the preview in the PR body.\n\nEffort: high (matching, a preview page, one batch command, MCP, tests).\n",
